2.3.m:
Thus has been recounted the deed of Śambhu, his going forth, a supreme festival;
now listen, O Nārada, to the auspicious event that took place in the city of the Himālaya.

Thus ends the fortieth chapter, named “Description of Śiva’s Journey,” in the Pārvatīkhaṇḍa, the third section of the second Rudrasaṃhitā of the glorious Śiva Mahāpurāṇa.

The women of the city said:
"The eyes of the inhabitants of Himavat's city have borne fruit;
whoever has seen this form, his birth has indeed achieved its purpose.
